{:en {:title "Kotoba native performance: Embench progress, updated 13 October 2026"
:description "Latest main Round 85: Kotoba takes 2.954× C execution time across all 19 workloads. The C-or-faster goal is unmet; optimization work has resumed."
:intro "Latest main integration and the complete Round 85 comparison are verified. Kotoba takes 2.954× C execution time in geometric mean. Optimization work has resumed; the objective remains unmet and unadopted candidates are preserved."
:notice "These are exploratory measurements of translated Kotoba programs using the upstream Embench speed driver and formula. They are not a certified official Kotoba Embench score, a released-toolchain result, or a claim of speed on other hosts."
:sections [{:title "Work resumed, objective unmet" :paragraphs ["Work resumed after the budget pause on 13 October. The adopted compiler remains integrated in main and the latest complete Round 85 ratio is 2.954× Kotoba execution time / C. No goal completion is claimed." "The revised generic two-argument fuel-register candidate preserves existing phase-loop and constant-table fast paths. Its initial producer passed all 483 original result/fuel/arena observations; changed fuel instructions, branch targets and scratch-register reads were checked. Three native self-build generations converged. All39 stabilized-producer images are identical to the tested initial images. Bootstrap transition attribution, generic boundary controls and performance measurement remain pending. The candidate is preserved without adoption and has no speed claim. Measurement snapshots below retain their state at measurement time; current work is active."]}
{:title "Latest main integration and Round 85 — 13 October 2026"
:paragraphs ["PR #1295 merged as 74b082f534d6326a5d5df9a0f415be1425b85aa6. All 19 CI checks passed; remote main ancestry, all 21 changed files, the 16-module source and native compiler artifact were read back and verified."
"The compiler reuses a checked vector descriptor after two fully certified scalar calls. Every read resets the count and tracked-slot writes invalidate it. Original index checks and traps remain; admission does not use workload names. The two picojpeg images retain the previously observed 1.8930% shorter fixed-slot timing, while the other 37 images are byte-identical to previous main. This individual exploratory observation is not a total-suite gain."
"Qualification passed three native self-build generations, 39 fresh images, the original 483 result/fuel/state observations, 54 generic pairs, 52 lookup controls and 34 policy refusals. There is no minimum 5% improvement cutoff."
"Fresh Round 85 accepted all 19 Kotoba and all 19 C measurements across 40 retained attempts. Normalized Kotoba execution time / C is 2.9542453261184902 (2.954×). Driver geometric scores are 12729.292501173408 for translated Kotoba and 37605.452876386684 for original C."
"The previous Round 84 ratio was 2.876720502080424. The larger ratio in this single cycle does not establish an overall improvement or a stable regression. C remains faster overall. Optimization work has resumed; the C-or-faster objective remains unmet. Raw CPU idle before/after and estimated background idle must each be at least 70%; only CPU-condition retries are allowed, at most three, selecting the first qualified sample rather than the fastest. The historical Round 84 and Round 83 records follow."]}
